.Dd October 22, 2026
.Dt JMON 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm jmon
.Nd nmon-style performance monitor with OpenTelemetry export
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl d
.Op Fl f
.Op Fl s Ar seconds
.Op Fl c Ar count
.Op Fl F Ar path
.Op Fl -show Ar keys
.Op Fl -otlp-endpoint Ar url
.Op Fl -prometheus Ar addr
.Op Fl -config Ar path
.Op Ar options ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
shows CPU, memory, disk, network, filesystem, process, jail, ZFS and sensor
statistics on an interactive screen modelled on
.Xr nmon 1 ,
and can export the same data as OpenTelemetry metrics over OTLP, as a
Prometheus scrape endpoint, and as nmon-compatible capture files.
All data comes from
.Xr sysctl 3 ,
.Xr getifaddrs 3 ,
.Xr getmntinfo 3
and
.Xr jail_get 2 ,
so no special privileges are needed.
.Pp
Without
.Fl d ,
.Fl f
or
.Fl -once ,
.Nm
runs interactively; any exporters given run at the same time.
.Ss Interactive keys
.Bl -tag -width "3, 4, 5" -compact
.It Cm c
CPU utilisation per processor; a
.Ql >
marks each CPU's peak since start
.It Cm C
compact CPU grid, for machines with many cores
.It Cm l
long-term CPU graph
.It Cm m
memory by page queue, ZFS ARC and swap
.It Cm V
virtual memory: faults by type, pager activity, page daemon
.It Cm L
superpage mappings, promotions and demotions
.It Cm k
load, run queue and blocked threads, context switches, interrupts,
system calls, faults
.It Cm d
disk throughput, operations, latency and queue depth
.It Cm G
also show partitions and other GEOM providers in the disk views
.It Cm g
disk groups (see
.Fl -disk-group )
.It Cm o
disk busy map, one cell per disk
.It Cm n
network interfaces
.It Cm T
TCP segments, retransmits, listen-queue overflows, connection states
.It Cm N
NFS client and server operations, retries and timeouts
.It Cm j
filesystems
.It Cm z
ZFS ARC hit ratio and pool capacity, health and I/O
.It Cm J
jails and
.Xr bhyve 8
virtual machines
.It Cm s
CPU temperature (current, hottest core, and session peak with its time),
clock, ACPI thermal zones, battery.
Temperatures turn yellow within 30\(de and red within 15\(de of the
CPU's throttle point
.It Cm R
reset the temperature peak
.It Cm t
top processes
.It Cm 3 , 4 , 5
sort top processes by CPU, memory or I/O
.It Cm a
show full command lines in the process list
.It Cm u
show only one user's processes
.It Cm /
search processes by command, arguments, user or jail
.It Cm \&.
hide idle CPUs, disks, interfaces and processes
.It Cm p
pause and resume
.It Cm w
start or stop an nmon recording in the record directory
.It Cm Up , Down , PgUp , PgDn , Home , End
scroll panels or the process list vertically
.It Cm v
checks: each statistic with an ok, warning or danger verdict
.It Cm 0
reset the CPU peak markers
.It Cm b
black and white
.It Cm + , -
double or halve the sampling interval
.It Cm r
system resources
.It Cm h
help
.It Ic ^L
redraw the screen.
jmon also redraws the whole screen every five seconds, which clears
kernel messages printed over it on the system console
.It Cm q
quit
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl s , Fl -interval Ar seconds
Seconds between samples.
Default 2.
.It Fl c , Fl -count Ar count
Exit after this many samples.
.It Fl d , Fl -daemon
Run without the screen, only collecting and exporting.
.It Fl -show Ar keys
Panels to open at start, given as screen keys, for example
.Ql cmdnt .
Also read from the
.Ev JMON
environment variable.
.It Fl f
Record to
.Pa <host>_<YYMMDD>_<HHMM>.nmon
in the record directory and run without the screen, like
.Ql nmon -f .
.It Fl F , Fl -record Ar path
Record samples to
.Ar path ,
or to standard output if
.Ar path
is
.Ql - .
.It Fl -record-format Cm nmon | jsonl
Format for recordings.
.Cm nmon
files can be loaded into nmon analyser or nmonchart.
.It Fl -record-dir Ar dir
Directory for
.Fl f
recordings.
.It Fl -rotate
With
.Fl f ,
start a new file every day at local midnight.
.It Fl -record-compress
With
.Fl -rotate ,
compress finished daily files with
.Xr gzip 1 .
The file being written when jmon stops is left uncompressed.
.It Fl -record-keep Ar days
With
.Fl -rotate ,
delete this host's recordings older than
.Ar days .
.It Fl -otlp-endpoint Ar url
Push metrics over OTLP, for example
.Ql http://collector:4317 .
Use an
.Ql https://
URL for TLS.
.It Fl -otlp-protocol Cm grpc | http/protobuf | http/json
OTLP transport.
Default
.Cm grpc .
.It Fl -otlp-interval Ar seconds
Seconds between OTLP exports.
Default 10.
.It Fl -otlp-ca Ar path
PEM file of additional CA certificates to trust for TLS.
.It Fl -prometheus Ar addr
Serve Prometheus metrics on
.Ar addr ,
for example
.Ql 0.0.0.0:9464 ,
at
.Pa /metrics .
.It Fl -disk-group Ar name Ns = Ns Ar disk Ns Op , Ns Ar disk ...
Define a disk group, shown with
.Cm g
and recorded as nmon
.Ql DG
sections.
Members may be disks or GEOM providers such as partitions.
Repeat the option for more groups.
.It Fl -export-top Ar n
Also export per-process metrics for the
.Ar n
busiest processes.
Off by default because process metrics have high cardinality.
.It Fl -once
Print one sample as JSON and exit.
.It Fl -config Ar path
Read options from a TOML file.
Default
.Pa /usr/local/etc/jmon.conf
if it exists.
.It Fl -syslog
Log to
.Xr syslog 3
with the daemon facility.
.It Fl -log-file Ar path
Append log messages to
.Ar path .
.El
.Sh CONFIGURATION FILE
The configuration file uses the long option names as keys.
Options given on the command line override the file.
Sending
.Dv SIGHUP
to jmon running without the screen (for example with
.Ql service jmon reload )
rereads the file and applies a new
.Cm interval
and
.Cm export-top ;
other changes need a restart.
With the screen up,
.Dv SIGHUP
stops jmon.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# /usr/local/etc/jmon.conf
interval = 10
otlp-endpoint = "https://collector.example.org:4317"
otlp-ca = "/usr/local/etc/ssl/collector-ca.pem"
prometheus = "127.0.0.1:9464"
export-top = 10
.Ed
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT
.It Ev JMON
Panels to open at start.
.It Ev JMON_CONFIG
Configuration file to read.
.It Ev NO_COLOR
Start in black and white.
.It Ev NMON_START , NMON_SNAP , NMON_END
Shell commands run at the start of an nmon recording, after each
snapshot (with the snapshot tag, such as
.Ql T0001 ,
as
.Li $1 ) ,
and at the end.
Their output is appended to the recording, so they can add their own
sections, as with
.Xr nmon 1 Ns 's
external data collectors.
.Ev JMON_START ,
.Ev JMON_SNAP
and
.Ev JMON_END
take precedence.
.It Ev JMON_LOG
Log filter, for example
.Ql debug .
.It Ev OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT
Enables OTLP export when no endpoint is given on the command line.
The other standard
.Ev OTEL_*
variables, such as
.Ev OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_HEADERS ,
.Ev OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_CERTIFICATE ,
.Ev OTEL_RESOURCE_ATTRIBUTES
and
.Ev OTEL_SERVICE_NAME ,
are honoured.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /usr/local/etc/rc.d/jmon -compact
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/jmon.conf
configuration file
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/rc.d/jmon
service script
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Watch CPU, memory, disks, network and top processes:
.Dl jmon --show cmdnt
.Pp
Run as a service exporting to a Collector:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
echo 'otlp-endpoint = "http://collector:4317"' > /usr/local/etc/jmon.conf
sysrc jmon_enable=YES
service jmon start
.Ed
.Pp
Record a day of one-minute samples to daily nmon files kept for a month:
.Dl jmon -f -s 60 --rotate --record-keep 30 --record-dir /var/log/jmon
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr netstat 1 ,
.Xr systat 1 ,
.Xr top 1 ,
.Xr gstat 8 ,
.Xr iostat 8 ,
.Xr vmstat 8
.Sh CAVEATS
CPU temperatures need the
.Xr coretemp 4
or
.Xr amdtemp 4
driver.
FreeBSD has no I/O wait time, so the nmon
.Ql Wait%
column is always zero.
ZFS pool capacity comes from
.Xr zpool 8
and is refreshed every 30 seconds, or every 5 seconds while the pool is
being written.
